# Prettier owns CODE formatting. It does not own PROSE.
#
# ── Markdown ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The same boundary arthome-core draws, for the same measured reason: Prettier
# pads every Markdown table cell to the column width, so a table whose cells hold
# sentences becomes source lines of several hundred characters — unreadable in an
# editor, and every later edit to one cell reflows the whole table so the diff no
# longer shows what changed. See code-conventions.md 5.1.
**/*.md

# ── Not ours to reformat ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# docs/arthome/ is a PROJECTION of arthome-core, rewritten by
#   `arthome-sync-agent-docs` on every install. Reformatting it here would put a
#   diff into `git status` at every install and destroy the one freshness signal
#   this design has: that a stale copy is the only thing that shows up there.
docs/arthome/

# The sibling packages, packed. Build output of another repository.
vendor/

# ── Generated or machine-owned ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# protobuf-es output. Reformatting it would produce a diff at every generation
# and say nothing about the wire.
libs/events/src/gen/
pnpm-lock.yaml
**/dist/
**/coverage/
**/generated/
node_modules/
